{"sounds":{"intro":"Sanskrit is written in Devanagari and spelled exactly as it sounds. The Latin line uses the scholars' IAST system, in which a bar over a vowel (ā) shows a long vowel, and a dot under a letter (ṭ, ṇ, ṣ) shows a retroflex sound with the tongue curled back. The third line is a simple English-style pronunciation. Sanskrit is a liturgical and scholarly language today, so the pronunciation follows the standard Indian tradition.","rows":[["a","like \"u\" in \"but\"","नमस्ते (namaste)"],["ā","like \"a\" in \"father\"","माता (mātā)"],["i / ī","\"i\" in \"bit\" / \"ee\" in \"see\"","पिता (pitā), नदी (nadī)"],["u / ū","\"u\" in \"put\" / \"oo\" in \"food\"","गुरुः (guruḥ), भूमिः (bhūmiḥ)"],["ṛ","a rolled \"ri\", like \"ri\" in \"rich\"","कृपया (kṛpayā)"],["e / o","long \"ay\" and long \"oh\"","देवः (devaḥ), लोकः (lokaḥ)"],["ai / au","like \"eye\" / like \"ow\"","शैलः (śailaḥ), गौः (gauḥ)"],["ṭ ḍ ṇ","tongue curled back, like in an Indian accent","पाठः (pāṭhaḥ)"],["kh gh ch jh th dh ph bh","the plain sound with a puff of air","भाषा (bhāṣā)"],["ś / ṣ","both like \"sh\"; ś is softer","शिष्यः (śiṣyaḥ)"],["ṃ","a nasal \"m\" or \"n\" at the end of a syllable","अहम् (ahaṃ)"],["ḥ","a soft breath \"h\" at the end (visarga)","रामः (rāmaḥ)"]],"notes":["Every Sanskrit word is said with its vowels. The vowel \"a\" is always said at the end of a syllable: \"rāma\" is RAH-mah, not \"Raam\".","This pool is much smaller than the Spanish one on purpose. Only common, well-attested words and forms are included. Nothing has been checked by a Sanskritist, so treat the forms as a first guide. Modern coinages are avoided."]},"numbers":[{"id":"0-to-10","title":"0 to 10","items":[["zero","śūnya","SHOO-nyah","शून्य"],["one","eka","AY-kah","एक"],["two","dvi","dvee","द्वि"],["three","tri","tree","त्रि"],["four","catur","CHAH-toor","चतुर्"],["five","pañca","PUN-chah","पञ्च"],["six","ṣaṭ","shut","षट्"],["seven","sapta","SUP-tah","सप्त"],["eight","aṣṭa","USH-tah","अष्ट"],["nine","nava","NUH-vah","नव"],["ten","daśa","DUH-shah","दश"]]},{"id":"bigger-numbers","title":"Bigger numbers","items":[["twenty","viṃśati","vim-SHAH-tee","विंशति"],["one hundred","śata","SHUH-tah","शत"],["one thousand","sahasra","SUH-huh-srah","सहस्र"]]}],"greetings":[{"id":"hello-and-goodbye","title":"Hello and goodbye","items":[["hello","namaste","NUH-muh-stay","नमस्ते"],["welcome","svāgatam","SWAH-guh-tum","स्वागतम्"],["good morning","suprabhātam","soo-PRUH-bah-tum","सुप्रभातम्"],["good night","śubha rātriḥ","SHOO-bhuh RAH-tree-huh","शुभरात्रिः"],["see you again","punar milāmaḥ","POO-nur mih-LAH-muh","पुनर्मिलामः"],["goodbye","punar darśanāya","POO-nur dur-shuh-NAH-yuh","पुनर्दर्शनाय"]]},{"id":"meeting-people","title":"Meeting people","items":[["how are you?","kuśalam","koo-SHUH-lum","कुशलम्?"],["I am well","aham kuśalī asmi","UH-hum koo-SHUH-lee UHS-mee","अहं कुशली अस्मि"],["what is your name?","tava nāma kim","TUH-vuh NAH-muh kim","तव नाम किम्?"],["my name is...","mama nāma","MUH-muh NAH-muh","मम नाम"],["where are you from?","kutaḥ āgataḥ asi","KOO-tuh AH-guh-tuh UH-see","कुतः आगतः असि?"],["I have come from England","aham āṅglāt āgataḥ","UH-hum ANG-glaht AH-guh-tuh","अहम् आङ्ग्लात् आगतः"]]}],"phrases":[{"id":"politeness","title":"Politeness","items":[["please","kṛpayā","KRIP-uh-yah","कृपया"],["thank you","dhanyavādaḥ","DHUN-yuh-vah-duh","धन्यवादः"],["sorry / forgive me","kṣamasva","KSHUH-muh-swuh","क्षमस्व"],["yes","āma","AH-muh","आम्"],["no","na","nuh","न"]]},{"id":"essential-phrases","title":"Essential phrases","items":[["I understand","aham jānāmi","UH-hum JAH-nah-mee","अहं जानामि"],["I do not understand","aham na jānāmi","UH-hum nuh JAH-nah-mee","अहं न जानामि"],["I know","jānāmi","JAH-nah-mee","जानामि"],["I want","icchāmi","ICH-chah-mee","इच्छामि"],["what is this?","etat kim","AY-tuh-t kim","एतत् किम्?"],["where?","kutra","KOO-trah","कुत्र?"],["I speak","vadāmi","vuh-DAH-mee","वदामि"],["I read","paṭhāmi","puh-TAH-mee","पठामि"],["I write","likhāmi","lih-KAH-mee","लिखामि"],["I see","paśyāmi","puh-SHYAH-mee","पश्यामि"],["I hear","śṛṇomi","SHRI-no-mee","शृणोमि"]]},{"id":"asking","title":"Asking","items":[["who?","kaḥ","kuh","कः?"],["what?","kim","kim","किम्?"],["where?","kutra","KOO-trah","कुत्र?"],["when?","kadā","kuh-DAH","कदा?"],["why?","kasmāt","kuhs-MAHT","कस्मात्?"],["how?","katham","kuh-THUM","कथम्?"]]}],"vocab":[{"id":"people-and-family","title":"People and family","items":[["mother","mātā","MAH-tah","माता"],["father","pitā","pih-TAH","पिता"],["son","putraḥ","POO-truh","पुत्रः"],["daughter","putrī","POO-tree","पुत्री"],["brother","bhrātā","BRAH-tah","भ्राता"],["sister","bhaginī","BHUH-gih-nee","भगिनी"],["friend","mitram","MIH-trum","मित्रम्"],["teacher","guruḥ","GOO-roo","गुरुः"],["student","śiṣyaḥ","SHISH-yuh","शिष्यः"],["king","rājā","RAH-jah","राजा"],["person","manuṣyaḥ","muh-NOOSH-yuh","मनुष्यः"],["boy","bālakaḥ","BAH-luh-kuh","बालकः"],["girl","bālikā","BAH-lih-kah","बालिका"]]},{"id":"food-and-nature","title":"Food and nature","items":[["water","jalam","JUH-lum","जलम्"],["food","annam","UN-num","अन्नम्"],["milk","dugdham","DOOG-dhum","दुग्धम्"],["fruit","phalam","PHUH-lum","फलम्"],["sun","sūryaḥ","SOO-ryuh","सूर्यः"],["moon","candraḥ","CHUN-druh","चन्द्रः"],["river","nadī","NUH-dee","नदी"],["mountain","parvataḥ","PUR-vuh-tuh","पर्वतः"],["forest","vanam","VUH-num","वनम्"],["horse","aśvaḥ","USH-vuh","अश्वः"],["cow","gauḥ","GOW-huh","गौः"],["animal","paśuḥ","PUH-shoo","पशुः"]]},{"id":"places-and-things","title":"Places and things","items":[["house","gṛham","GRI-hum","गृहम्"],["city","nagaram","NUH-guh-rum","नगरम्"],["book","pustakam","POOS-tuh-kum","पुस्तकम्"],["knowledge","vidyā","VID-yah","विद्या"],["god","devaḥ","DAY-vuh","देवः"],["language","bhāṣā","BHAH-shah","भाषा"],["word","śabdaḥ","SHUB-duh","शब्दः"]]},{"id":"describing","title":"Describing","items":[["big","bṛhat","BRI-hut","बृहत्"],["small","laghu","LUH-ghoo","लघु"],["beautiful","sundara","SOON-duh-ruh","सुन्दर"],["good","uttama","OOT-tuh-muh","उत्तम"],["difficult","kaṭhina","KUH-tih-nuh","कठिन"],["easy","sarala","SUH-ruh-luh","सरल"],["new","nava","NUH-vuh","नव"],["old","purāṇa","poo-RAH-nuh","पुराण"]]},{"id":"verbs-he-she-does","title":"Verbs (he / she does)","items":[["is","asti","UHS-tee","अस्ति"],["goes","gacchati","GUH-chuh-tee","गच्छति"],["comes","āgacchati","AH-guh-chuh-tee","आगच्छति"],["eats","khādati","KHAH-duh-tee","खादति"],["drinks","pibati","PIH-buh-tee","पिबति"],["gives","dadāti","DUH-dah-tee","ददाति"],["does / makes","karoti","KUH-ro-tee","करोति"],["asks","pṛcchati","PRIK-chuh-tee","पृच्छति"],["speaks","vadati","VUH-duh-tee","वदति"]]}],"grammar":[{"id":"pronouns","title":"Pronouns","text":["Sanskrit verbs show the person, so the pronoun is often left out. The third person has three genders: saḥ (he), sā (she), tat (it). The polite \"you\" is \"bhavān\" (to a man) and \"bhavatī\" (to a woman)."],"rows":[["I","aham","अहम्"],["you (one)","tvam","त्वम्"],["he","saḥ","सः"],["she","sā","सा"],["we","vayam","वयम्"],["you (plural)","yūyam","यूयम्"],["they (m)","te","ते"]],"ex":[["I am a student","aham śiṣyaḥ asmi","UH-hum SHISH-yuh UHS-mee","अहं शिष्यः अस्मि"],["you are a teacher","tvam guruḥ asi","TWUM GOO-roo UH-see","त्वं गुरुः असि"],["he is a boy","saḥ bālakaḥ asti","SUH BAH-luh-kuh UHS-tee","सः बालकः अस्ति"],["she is a girl","sā bālikā asti","SAH BAH-lih-kah UHS-tee","सा बालिका अस्ति"],["we are friends","vayam mitrāṇi smaḥ","VUH-yum MIH-trah-nee SMUH","वयं मित्राणि स्मः"]]},{"id":"to-be-as","title":"To be: as","text":["The present of \"to be\" is: asmi (I am), asi (you are), asti (he, she is), smaḥ (we are), stha (you are, plural), santi (they are)."],"rows":[["I am","asmi","अस्मि"],["you are","asi","असि"],["he / she is","asti","अस्ति"],["we are","smaḥ","स्मः"],["you are (plural)","stha","स्थ"],["they are","santi","सन्ति"]],"ex":[["I am here","aham atra asmi","UH-hum UH-trah UHS-mee","अहम् अत्र अस्मि"],["you are good","tvam uttamaḥ asi","TWUM OOT-tuh-muh UH-see","त्वम् उत्तमः असि"],["the book is on the table","pustakam māñce asti","POOS-tuh-kum MAHN-chay UHS-tee","पुस्तकं माञ्चे अस्ति"]]},{"id":"negation","title":"Negation","text":["Put \"na\" before the verb. \"Mā\" with a command means \"do not\"."],"rows":[["not","na","न"],["do not (command)","mā","मा"]],"ex":[["I know","jānāmi","JAH-nah-mee","जानामि"],["I do not know","na jānāmi","nuh JAH-nah-mee","न जानामि"],["he goes","gacchati","GUH-chuh-tee","गच्छति"],["he does not go","na gacchati","nuh GUH-chuh-tee","न गच्छति"],["do not go","mā gaccha","MAH GUH-chuh","मा गच्छ"]]},{"id":"commands","title":"Commands","text":["The second-person command is the bare stem: gaccha (go), paśya (see), śṛṇu (listen)."],"rows":[["go!","gaccha","गच्छ"],["come!","āgaccha","आगच्छ"],["see!","paśya","पश्य"],["listen!","śṛṇu","शृणु"]],"ex":[["come here","atra āgaccha","UH-trah AH-guh-chuh","अत्र आगच्छ"],["look","paśya","PUH-shyuh","पश्य"],["listen","śṛṇu","SHRI-noo","शृणु"],["read","paṭha","PUH-tuh","पठ"]]}],"name":"Sanskrit","id":"sa","flag":"in","script":"Devanagari","note":""}